WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.615
A content delivery network places caching proxies
near users.

00:00:03.615 --> 00:00:05.808
The origin owns the original content.

00:00:05.808 --> 00:00:10.193
A fresh cache hit lets an edge answer without
fetching that content again.

00:00:10.193 --> 00:00:11.734
A miss reaches the origin.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:16.297
Cache policy determines what may be stored and when
a response can be reused.

00:00:16.297 --> 00:00:18.594
Read the whole Cache-Control policy.

00:00:18.594 --> 00:00:22.741
Public max-age sixty can permit shared caching for
sixty seconds.

00:00:22.741 --> 00:00:29.122
Private max-age sixty permits a private browser
cache, but excludes storage of the whole response in

00:00:29.122 --> 00:00:30.334
a shared CDN cache.

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:34.545
No-cache can permit storage, but requires validation
before reuse.

00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:36.268
No-store prohibits storage.

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:39.331
Max-age zero makes a response immediately stale.

00:00:39.363 --> 00:00:44.279
Anycast uses routing announcements from multiple
sites for the same address prefix.

00:00:44.279 --> 00:00:47.891
BGP selects a route according to network policy and
topology.

00:00:47.891 --> 00:00:51.918
The selected site is not necessarily the
geographically closest one.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:57.721
DNS steering and anycast operate at different points
in the request path and can be used together.

00:00:57.721 --> 00:01:00.033
Anycast is used for more than UDP DNS.

00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:05.871
Stateful connections need careful engineering
because a route change can shift traffic to a site

00:01:05.871 --> 00:01:07.635
without the connection state.

00:01:07.635 --> 00:01:13.291
Likewise, caching and extra workers do not solve
concurrent seat allocation in a registration

00:01:13.291 --> 00:01:13.778
service.

00:01:13.778 --> 00:01:19.799
Finish the unit by explaining which layer handles
discovery, worker selection, caching, and correct

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:21.197
updates to shared data.
